card-presentation.patch binds printing, physical foil and validated cosmetic
settings by player, section and entry position at physical object creation,
before library shuffling. A stable-instance table survives zone changes and
checkpoints. Created copies have new stable identifiers and use defaults.
Visible Manabrew DTOs read that table; hidden and face-down cards never receive
presentation metadata. Redacted checkpoints omit hidden associations.
The existing private encrypted room transport and public-state paths are used.
Stack appearance uses stable source identifiers and visibility-filtered source
objects, not card names. Token overrides are not supported: the pinned engine
does not expose an authoritative association to Forge token-script identities.
Same-session reconnect can resend state with pinned peer keys; a hard-reloaded
guest cannot replace its old pinned key through this integration.
Build with node scripts/build-ironsmith.mjs. Requires rustup, Cargo, Git, tar
and network access on first build. The script installs pinned Rust and wasm-pack
tools into its build environment. Unchanged source, patch and script inputs
reuse generated output.
No upstream tests or verification scripts run as part of this package build.

The pinned upstream tree and npm manifest do not declare a source-code license
or contain a root license file. This package records provenance, not a license
grant. Confirm upstream redistribution permission before publishing modified
engine artifacts. The local integration is private and does not vendor the
upstream source. Card data and artwork retain their separate rights.
